# Git Commit Messages

Write all git commit messages in English.

## Format

- Use imperative mood, present tense (e.g. "Add", "Fix", "Update", "Remove").
- Keep the subject line concise (under ~72 characters).
- Optionally add a blank line followed by a body explaining the "why".

## Examples

```text
Add login trend chart to overview

Fix MFA disable flow when policy is enforced

Update docs to reflect x-request-id and consent changes
```

Do not use Chinese (or any other non-English language) in commit messages, commit bodies, or PR titles/descriptions.
